{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>She was being brought out.</b> To be burned. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted from here: it is better for a person to cast himself into a fiery furnace rather than whiten the face of his fellow in public; for thus Tamar said: if he acknowledges, well and good; and if not, I am casting myself into the fiery furnace and I will not whiten his face. And even though the word מוצאת is spelled with an alef, it can be interpreted according to this midrash from the language of (Lamentations 4:11): ״וצית אש בציון״. And you will find the special Name in the initial letters in sequence: ויאמר י\"הודה ה\"וציאוה ו\"תשרף ה\"יא מוצאת — to make known that at the time Judah was planning her burning, the Holy One, blessed be He, was planning salvation and mercy, and all causes come from Him, blessed be He." "<b>And she sent to her father-in-law, saying.</b> That is, that the messengers should say to him in her name: 'To the man to whom these belong, I am with child.' For they themselves would not have known what was in her hand, and she did this so as not to shame him. And when she saw that he did not acknowledge this, and thought that perhaps he had forgotten the matter, she said to him herself, face to face: 'Recognize, please, whose seal…' and so on; and therefore she mentioned them by name. And still her intention was that if he acknowledged this, well and good, and if not, she would be burned and would not whiten his face." "<b>And in the Jerusalem Targum</b> of <b>she was being brought out</b>, it mentions that Samael hid them so that she would not find them and be burned, and Tamar sought mercy before the Holy One, blessed be He, to provide her with three, and three would be saved, and then she would give the three to him; and the Holy One, blessed be He, hinted to Gabriel and he returned them to her, and she cast them at the feet of the judges; and this is what she said to him: <b>Recognize, please, whose are the seal, the cords, and the staff.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:45.046988843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}